  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Pi Shui Han vents after escaping life chasing fire, the battle draws in two rank six peak Gu Immortals: Qie Shi Min of the enslavement path and Half Moon Brutemaster of the moon path. They have pretty good relationships with a certain demonic path Gu Immortal, so they intervene and mediate, and push Pi Shui Han toward Dong Fang tribe’s main camp instead of Tai Qiu. At Jade Pool blessed land he sends three huge desolate beast birds from his immortal aperture to encircle Fang Yuan’s group.",
      "chapters": [
        795
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_pi_shui_han",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_half_moon_brutemaster",
        "fac_dong_fang_tribe",
        "loc_tai_qiu",
        "loc_jade_pool_blessed_land",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Beside Half Moon Brutemaster he looks much inferior to Pi Shui Han once Fairy Li Shan and Hei Lou Lan reveal their strength, and both regret attacking before reading the field. He asks Fang Yuan to return the three desolate birds. Fang Yuan tosses them back. He has other techniques that could raise those birds’ battle strength by fifty percent, but he does not use them.",
      "chapters": [
        796
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "jade-pool-scramble",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_li_shan",
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dong Fang Chang Fan sees the enslavement path Gu Immortal using a unique method to capture Dong Fang tribe’s Gu Masters among demonic path Gu Immortals scavenging Jade Pool blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        801
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "captives",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_dong_fang_chang_fan",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He sits on a chariot that is his movement killer move and gives off the aura of Immortal Gu. His expression is grim. He has a weaker body than normal immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        804
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He keeps Dong Fang tribe captives in his immortal aperture and kills them during the chase to force Dong Fang Chang Fan to lose control. A ray of starlight grazes Fang Yuan’s shoulder and pierces Qie Shi Min’s forehead. His expression freezes in disbelief. His head explodes, the chariot disassembles, and he falls. Because he was chasing fervently he was slightly careless, and he is killed in one move.",
      "chapters": [
        804
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Northern Plains, at the place where he died, Gu Immortals try to find Immortal Gu aura in the air. Some try to enter the blessed land that formed from his immortal aperture, and leave after failing.",
      "chapters": [
        811
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-aperture",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    }
  ],
